WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.910
Part ten: the review. Every figure in Anil's return, where it came from - and anything he types over it, marked as his.

2
00:00:10.531 --> 00:00:15.021
Salary from Form 16, with the source beside it.

3
00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:24.830
His residential status, from the days he was in India. A resident: all his income counts, wherever it arose.

4
00:00:25.422 --> 00:00:37.832
Arrears for 2022-23 were paid to him this year. That year's income and regime give the relief under section 89 - with a reminder to file Form 10 E.

5
00:00:38.453 --> 00:00:49.083
Income and assets outside India have their own cards. And his minor son's interest is added to his income, less the exemption for each child.

6
00:00:49.688 --> 00:00:59.818
A flat he owns half of, with his wife, let out: rent, municipal tax and loan interest, each taken by his fifty percent share.

7
00:01:00.422 --> 00:01:06.802
Online-game winnings and a crypto sale: taxed at thirty percent, whatever his slab.

8
00:01:07.422 --> 00:01:13.732
Self-assessment tax he paid himself, with the B S R code and challan number.

9
00:01:14.343 --> 00:01:24.283
Capital gains: the four sales read from the C A M S statement - one grandfathered to January 2018 - and a plot he typed.

10
00:01:24.906 --> 00:01:42.066
The plot was bought in 2010. Twelve and a half percent without indexation, or twenty percent with it: SimplyFile works out both and takes the cheaper. Twenty lakh went into 54 E C bonds, so that much is exempt.

11
00:01:42.672 --> 00:01:49.532
A short-term loss from 2024-25, set off against this year's gains.

12
00:01:50.125 --> 00:02:00.465
Two gifts: two lakh from an uncle - a relative, so it is free - and seventy-five thousand from a friend: over fifty thousand in the year, so it is income.

13
00:02:01.063 --> 00:02:10.373
Deductions from Form 16 - and more for the old regime, 80 D D to 80 G G C, with what each schedule asks for.

14
00:02:10.985 --> 00:02:21.565
A few questions last: his contact details, and his share of farm income - forty thousand. It is exempt, but it is shown in the return.

15
00:02:22.172 --> 00:02:27.092
File: with capital gains, his form is I T R 2.

16
00:02:27.703 --> 00:02:39.203
The department's JSON, checked against its own schema - valid. He downloads it and uploads it on the e-filing portal: SimplyFile never files for him.

17
00:02:39.813 --> 00:02:50.853
Once filed, he notes the acknowledgement. And for an earlier year he missed something in, the updated return - I T R U - is worked out here too.

18
00:02:51.468 --> 00:02:58.308
Next, part eleven: the same screen for a CA firm's families and consultants.
